[08:51:00] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a5f3b9e3cd4fefc1","toolName":"read","result":"<file path=\"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\.coda\\skills\\planning-epics\\references\\backlog-template.md\" lines=\"416\" start=\"1\" end=\"300\" returned=\"300\" has_more=\"true\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Agent-Native Epics Backlog Template\n     2|\n     3|## Template Rules\n     4|- **No prose.** Every section is structured data only.\n     5|- **No value propositions.** No \"why this matters\" narrative.\n     6|- **No meeting agendas.** Governance content is humanize-spec responsibility.\n     7|- **Name the thing, not just its id.** Machine id references — every column named `id`,\n     8|  `item_id`, `prd_id`, `blocked`, `blocker`, or ending in `_id`, `_ids` — carry bare ids\n     9|  only, because the dependency graph and the downstream projection parse them positionally.\n    10|  EVERYWHERE ELSE an id appears — `theme`, `personas`, `topological_order`,\n    11|  `phase_mapping`, `scope`, `reason`, `description`, `unaligned_reason`,\n    12|  `recommendation`, `mitigation`, and every prose slot — the id is followed by the item's\n    13|  short name in parentheses: `EPIC-03 (shared auth contract)`. Names come verbatim from\n    14|  the item's own definition heading, or from the PRD heading for a PRD id. A bare id\n    15|  outside the machine columns is a defect, not a shorthand.\n    16|  **This includes fields ending in `_refs` and the `fr`/`jtbd`/`kpi` lists inside an\n    17|  epic's `traceability` block — `themes.fr_refs`, `rsk_refs`, `asm_refs`, and\n    18|  `traceability.fr`/`.jtbd`/`.kpi` are NOT exempt.** Every id in those lists is followed\n    19|  by `(name)`, copied verbatim from that id's own `prd_id_ownership.prd_name` row — a\n    20|  lookup, not new prose, so this adds a few words per id, not a sentence. The `blocked`/\n    21|  `blocker` id columns in `## dependencies` and `ordering_proof` stay bare (the graph\n    22|  parses them), but each gains a sibling `blocked_description`/`blocker_description`\n    23|  column carrying the same kind of name. A value of `—` (no reference) has nothing to\n    24|  describe and stays `—`.\n    25|- **All items carry status.** `complete` | `pending` | `assumption` | `unaligned`.\n    26|- **All gaps appear in open_questions.** Single registry, no scatter.\n    27|- **PRD open questions are never re-listed.** They arrive in the prompt's `## OPEN QUESTIONS` /\n    28|  `## PROJECT DECISIONS` blocks; cite their ids where an epic relies on one.\n    29|- **Language:** Generate in DETECTED_LANGUAGE. Section headers in English always.\n    30|- **Single file output.** ALL sections below go into ONE file (EPICS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md).\n    31|  Do NOT split sections into separate batch files. Do NOT use Write-Flush-Forget.\n    32|  If context is tight, reduce detail density — never split the file.\n    33|\n    34|---\n    35|\n    36|## Spec File Structure\n    37|\n    38|`{project_name}` below is the **sanitized** value produced by the Parameter Sanitization step in SKILL.md — newlines, `#`, `|`, and backtick characters stripped, length capped at 120 chars. Never substitute the raw parameter.\n    39|\n    40|```markdown\n    41|# {project_name} — Epics Backlog Spec\n    42|version: {NEW_VERSION}\n    43|session: {SESSION_ID}\n    44|mode: {BUILD | REPAIR}\n    45|date: {ISO 8601}\n    46|language: {DETECTED_LANGUAGE}\n    47|prd_source: {prd_spec_file_path}\n    48|contract_format: structured\n    49|prd_source_hash: {sha256 from PRD content_hash or computed over PRD-SPEC content}\n    50|status: {draft | complete}\n    51|\n    52|---\n    53|\n    54|**`*_source_hash`: transcribe it, or RUN it — never estimate it.** When the\n    55|upstream artifact declares a `content_hash`, copy that value character for\n    56|character. When it declares none, compute one over the upstream file with the\n    57|recipe in `execution-protocol.md` §10.5.4. A sha256 cannot be produced by\n    58|inspection, and downstream validation checks only that the value is 64 lowercase\n    59|hex characters, so a fabricated hash passes review and mis-pins the source.\n    60|\n    61|## project_info\n    62|client_name: {client_name}\n    63|project_name: {project_name}\n    64|project_description: {project_description}\n    65|\n    66|---\n    67|\n    68|## prd_id_ownership\n    69|\n    70|Complete projection of PRD IDs into the epic layer. Every PRD ID from\n    71|functional requirements, non-functional requirements, JTBDs, KPIs, risks,\n    72|assumptions, dependencies, personas, and literal_registry is represented exactly\n    73|once as `owned`, `cross_cutting`, or `deferred`.\n    74|\n    75|| prd_id | prd_name | type | disposition | epic_ids | phase | reason | source_ref |\n    76||--------|----------|------|-------------|----------|-------|--------|------------|\n    77|| FR-01 | {requirement_statement, short} | FR | owned | EPIC-01 | phase_1_mvp | primary deliverable of EPIC-01 ({epic_title}) | PRD:FR-01 |\n    78|| RSK-01 | {risk_statement, short} | risk | cross_cutting | EPIC-01, EPIC-03 | all | affects the sign-in path (EPIC-01) and reporting (EPIC-03) | PRD:RSK-01 |\n    79|| ASM-02 | {assumption_statement, short} | assumption | deferred | — | deferred | unresolved upstream assumption blocks delivery | PRD:ASM-02 |\n    80|| LIT-01 | {literal_name} | literal | owned | EPIC-01 | phase_1_mvp | exact value used by the acceptance criteria of FR-01 ({name}) | PRD:LIT-01 |\n    81|\n    82|`prd_name` is copied from the PRD heading that defines the id. This table is the whole\n    83|projection of the PRD into the backlog — read as bare ids it is unauditable by the person\n    84|who wrote the PRD.\n    85|\n    86|---\n    87|\n    88|## themes\n    89|\n    90|### T-01: {theme_name}\n    91|- features:\n    92|  - {feature_name} | fr_refs: FR-01 ({fr_name}), FR-03 ({fr_name}) | priority: must_have\n    93|  - {feature_name} | fr_refs: FR-05 ({fr_name}) | priority: should_have\n    94|- status: {complete | assumption}\n    95|\n    96|### T-02: {theme_name}\n    97|- features:\n    98|  - {feature_name} | fr_refs: FR-02 ({fr_name}) | priority: must_have\n    99|  - {feature_name} | fr_refs: FR-04 ({fr_name}), FR-06 ({fr_name}) | priority: could_have | [ASM: inferred grouping]\n   100|- status: assumption\n   101|\n   102|---\n   103|\n   104|## epics\n   105|\n   106|> **EPIC ID ORDER IS NOT BUILD ORDER.** Ids reflect authoring sequence; foundational\n   107|> enablers are routinely numbered last. The authoritative execution order for every\n   108|> downstream consumer (sprint planning, decomposition, implementation) is\n   109|> `## sequencing → topological_order`, with its edge table in `## dependencies` —\n   110|> both are at the END of this file. Do not derive a sequence from the epic list\n   111|> below.\n   112|\n   113|### EPIC-01: {epic_title}\n   114|- type: feature\n   115|- theme: T-01 ({theme_name})\n   116|- personas: P-01 ({role_name}), P-02 ({role_name})\n   117|- priority_tier: must_have\n   118|- complexity: M\n   119|- traceability:\n   120|  - fr: FR-01 ({fr_name}), FR-03 ({fr_name})\n   121|  - jtbd: JTBD-01 ({jtbd_name})\n   122|  - kpi: KPI-01 ({kpi_name})\n   123|- nfr_dod:\n   124|  - NFR-01: {target}\n   125|  - NFR-03: {target}\n   126|- rsk_refs: RSK-01 ({risk_name})\n   127|- asm_refs: ASM-01 ({assumption_name})\n   128|- scope:\n   129|  - in: {what this epic delivers}\n   130|  - out: {what is excluded}\n   131|- status: complete\n   132|\n   133|### EPIC-02: {epic_title}\n   134|- type: feature\n   135|- theme: T-01 ({theme_name})\n   136|- personas: P-01 ({role_name})\n   137|- priority_tier: should_have\n   138|- complexity: L\n   139|- traceability:\n   140|  - fr: FR-05 ({fr_name}), FR-06 ({fr_name})\n   141|  - jtbd: JTBD-02 ({jtbd_name})\n   142|  - kpi: —\n   143|- nfr_dod:\n   144|  - NFR-02: {target}\n   145|- rsk_refs: —\n   146|- asm_refs: ASM-02 ({assumption_name})\n   147|- scope:\n   148|  - in: {scope}\n   149|  - out: {exclusions}\n   150|- status: complete\n   151|\n   152|### EPIC-03: {enabler_title}\n   153|- type: enabler\n   154|- theme: T-02 ({theme_name})\n   155|- personas: P-03 ({role_name})\n   156|- priority_tier: must_have\n   157|- complexity: S\n   158|- traceability:\n   159|  - fr: —\n   160|  - kpi: KPI-02 ({kpi_name})\n   161|- nfr_dod: —\n   162|- rsk_refs: —\n   163|- asm_refs: —\n   164|- scope:\n   165|  - in: {scope}\n   166|  - out: {exclusions}\n   167|- status: unaligned\n   168|- unaligned_reason: no FR match\n   169|\n   170|### SPIKE-01: {investigation_title}\n   171|- type: spike\n   172|- goal: {investigation objective}\n   173|- prerequisite_for: EPIC-02 ({epic_title})\n   174|- traceability:\n   175|  - fr: FR-05 ({fr_name})\n   176|- complexity: S\n   177|- status: complete\n   178|\n   179|---\n   180|\n   181|## dependencies\n   182|\n   183|| blocked | blocked_description | blocker | blocker_description | type | impact | mitigation |\n   184||---------|----------------------|--------|----------------------|------|--------|------------|\n   185|| EPIC-01 | {epic_title} | EPIC-03 | {epic_title} | epic_to_epic | {consequence} | {strategy} |\n   186|| EPIC-02 | {epic_title} | — | — | none | — | — |\n   187|| EPIC-03 | {epic_title} | — | — | none | — | — |\n   188|| EPIC-04 | {epic_title} | EXT:vendor_api | {dependency_name} | external | {consequence} | {fallback} |\n   189|| SPIKE-01 | {investigation_title} | EPIC-01 | {epic_title} | epic_to_epic | {consequence} | {strategy} |\n   190|\n   191|`blocked_description`/`blocker_description` are copied verbatim from the blocked/blocker item's\n   192|own title (EPIC/SPIKE/ENABLER) or from `prd_id_ownership.prd_name` (external `DEP-XX` refs). A `—`\n   193|blocker has nothing to describe and stays `—`.\n   194|\n   195|### circular_resolutions\n   196|(If circular dependencies were detected and resolved)\n   197|\n   198|- cycle: EPIC-XX <-> EPIC-YY\n   199|  - resolved_by: ENABLER-NNN\n   200|  - interface: {shared contract name}\n   201|  - new_chain: ENABLER-NNN → EPIC-XX, ENABLER-NNN → EPIC-YY\n   202|\n   203|(If no cycles detected)\n   204|- none\n   205|\n   206|---\n   207|\n   208|## sequencing\n   209|\n   210|> **This section is the authoritative build order.** Downstream planners MUST adopt\n   211|> `topological_order` as given (restricted to the units in their scope, relative\n   212|> positions preserved) rather than re-deriving a sequence from the epic list or from\n   213|> id numbers. Re-derivation is how ordering contradictions get introduced.\n   214|\n   215|### topological_order\n   216|1. EPIC-03 — {enabler_title} (enabler, no blockers)\n   217|2. ENABLER-NNN — {title} (if created by circular resolution)\n   218|3. EPIC-01 — {epic_title} (blocked by EPIC-03)\n   219|4. SPIKE-01 — {investigation_title} (blocked by EPIC-01)\n   220|5. EPIC-02 — {epic_title} (blocked by SPIKE-01)\n   221|\n   222|### phase_mapping\n   223|(Derived from PRD mvp_phasing + dependency constraints)\n   224|\n   225|The phase label leads so the parentheses stay free for titles. This list and\n   226|`topological_order` are what a Product Owner reads to understand what gets built when;\n   227|a sequence of bare ids does not answer that question.\n   228|\n   229|- phase_1_mvp (must_have, no/resolved blockers): EPIC-03 ({enabler_title}), EPIC-01 ({epic_title})\n   230|- phase_2 (should_have): EPIC-02 ({epic_title}), SPIKE-01 ({investigation_title})\n   231|- phase_3 (could_have): EPIC-04 ({epic_title})\n   232|- deferred: {PRD out_of_scope items and wont_have FRs, each named}\n   233|\n   234|### sequencing_validations\n   235|- edges_checked: {N} of {N} rows in `## dependencies` (epic_to_epic edges; external\n   236|  rows are carried, not ordered)\n   237|- blocked_before_blocker_violations: {0 | N — auto-corrected}\n   238|- prd_conflict_notes: {none | list of PRD phasing conflicts}\n   239|\n   240|#### ordering_proof\n   241|(One row per epic_to_epic edge, checked against `topological_order` above. A bare\n   242|violation count is an assertion; this table is the evidence. Emit every row — a\n   243|proof covering only the interesting edges is not a proof.)\n   244|\n   245|| blocked | blocked_description | blocker | blocker_description | blocker_position | blocked_position | ok |\n   246||---------|----------------------|--------|----------------------|-------------------|-------------------|-----|\n   247|| EPIC-01 | {epic_title} | EPIC-03 | {epic_title} | 1 | 3 | yes |\n   248|\n   249|---\n   250|\n   251|## reclassification_log\n   252|\n   253|| candidate | gate_failed | reclassified_as | redistributed_to | reason |\n   254||-----------|-------------|-----------------|-------------------|--------|\n   255|| Logging system | gate_2_nfr | dod_constraint | EPIC-03, EPIC-07 | NFR-04 overlap |\n   256|| Tech spike: auth | gate_1_demo | SPIKE-01 | — | Research/exploration |\n   257|| API documentation | gate_3_enabler | enabler EPIC-03 | — | Tooling, traces to KPI-02 |\n   258|\n   259|---\n   260|\n   261|## persona_coverage\n   262|\n   263|| persona | persona_name | epic_count | epic_ids | status |\n   264||---------|--------------|-----------|----------|--------|\n   265|| P-01 | {role_name} | 3 | EPIC-01, EPIC-02, EPIC-04 | covered |\n   266|| P-02 | {role_name} | 1 | EPIC-01 | covered |\n   267|| P-03 | {role_name} | 0 | — | uncovered |\n   268|\n   269|---\n   270|\n   271|## goal_coverage\n   272|\n   273|| prd_goal | epic_ids | status |\n   274||----------|----------|--------|\n   275|| Goal 1 | EPIC-01, EPIC-02 | covered |\n   276|| Goal 2 | EPIC-04 | covered |\n   277|| Goal 3 | — | uncovered |\n   278|\n   279|---\n   280|\n   281|## open_questions\n   282|\n   283|### pending_inputs\n   284|\n   285|| id | affected_ids | blocking | type | section | item_id | field | impact | question | fallback_behavior | source_ref |\n   286||----|--------------|----------|------|---------|---------|-------|--------|----------|-------------------|------------|\n   287|| PI-01 | {EPIC-02, FR-05} | {yes | no} | missing | epics | EPIC-02 | complexity | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | {needed answer} | {BLOCKED or narrowest safe behavior} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   288|| PI-02 | {EPIC-04, DEP-02} | yes | missing | dependencies | EPIC-04 | mitigation | HIGH | {needed fallback} | BLOCKED | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   289|\n   290|### alignment_gaps\n   291|\n   292|| id | affected_ids | blocking | type | item_id | impact | description | fallback_behavior | source_ref |\n   293||----|--------------|----------|------|---------|--------|-------------|-------------------|------------|\n   294|| AG-01 | {EPIC-03, KPI-02} | no | unaligned_epic | EPIC-03 | MEDIUM | No FR match, traces only to KPI-02 | Keep as enabler if KPI-backed | EPICS:EPIC-03 |\n   295|| AG-02 | {Goal 3} | {yes | no} | uncovered_goal | Goal 3 | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | No epic addresses this goal | {defer or BLOCKED} | PRD:goal_3 |\n   296|| AG-03 | {P-03} | {yes | no} | uncovered_persona | P-03 | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | No epics mapped to this persona | {defer or BLOCKED} | PRD:P-03 |\n   297|\n   298|### assumptions_to_validate\n   299|\n   300|| id | affected_ids | blocking | assumption | source | impact_if_wrong | validation_method | fallback_behavior |\n</file>","isError":false,"durationMs":16}}
