[08:51:03] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bed162b25b4c9b32","toolName":"read","result":"<file path=\"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\.coda\\skills\\planning-epics\\references\\backlog-template.md\" lines=\"416\" start=\"300\" end=\"416\" returned=\"117\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n   300|| id | affected_ids | blocking | assumption | source | impact_if_wrong | validation_method | fallback_behavior |\n   301||----|--------------|----------|------------|--------|-----------------|-------------------|-------------------|\n   302|| ASM-E01 | {T-02, EPIC-XX} | no | T-02 grouping inferred | theme generation | Features may be misgrouped | Review with domain expert | Use current grouping until reviewed |\n   303|\n   304|### summary\n   305|- total_themes: {N}\n   306|- total_epics: {N}\n   307|- total_enablers: {N}\n   308|- total_spikes: {N}\n   309|- total_reclassified: {N}\n   310|- unaligned_epics: {N}\n   311|- uncovered_goals: {N}\n   312|- uncovered_personas: {N}\n   313|- pending_inputs: {N}\n   314|- assumptions: {N}\n   315|- status: {draft | complete}\n   316|```\n   317|\n   318|Upstream open questions are delivered by Stepwise's `## OPEN QUESTIONS` prompt block and settled ones by `## PROJECT DECISIONS`; cite their ids in the body where your work relies on them. Never re-list them here or in `_open_questions`.\n   319|\n   320|---\n   321|\n   322|## Generation Rules\n   323|\n   324|### Section Ordering\n   325|Generate sections in this order:\n   326|prd_id_ownership → themes → epics (with qualification gates) → dependencies (with circular resolution) →\n   327|sequencing → reclassification_log → persona_coverage → goal_coverage → open_questions.\n   328|\n   329|Dependencies MUST come after all epics are qualified (including enablers created\n   330|by reclassification). Sequencing MUST come after dependencies (uses the graph).\n   331|`prd_id_ownership` is generated before themes/epics and is the authoritative\n   332|projection map for downstream research. open_questions is ALWAYS LAST —\n   333|consolidates from all prior sections.\n   334|\n   335|### Epic Qualification (During Generation)\n   336|\n   337|Process every FR-derived candidate through gates sequentially.\n   338|A candidate that fails a gate is reclassified, NOT discarded.\n   339|\n   340|**Gate 1 — Discrete Deliverable:**\n   341|Can the team demo this independently?\n   342|- NO + research/exploration → SPIKE-XX\n   343|- NO + quality/process → DoD constraint on parent epic\n   344|\n   345|**Gate 2 — NFR Overlap:**\n   346|Does candidate scope equal a PRD NFR?\n   347|- YES → DoD constraint on the functional epic(s) it supports\n   348|- Add NFR-XX and target to the functional epic's nfr_dod field\n   349|\n   350|**Gate 3 — Enabler vs Feature:**\n   351|Is this documentation, infrastructure, or tooling?\n   352|- YES → type: enabler. Trace to KPI (not FR).\n   353|- No KPI or FR traceability → status: unaligned\n   354|\n   355|**All decisions → reclassification_log entry.**\n   356|\n   357|### Dependency Graph Construction\n   358|1. For each EPIC-XX: identify all blockers (epic-to-epic, technical, external, resource)\n   359|2. Every epic MUST appear in the table (including \"none\" dependencies)\n   360|3. Circular detection: scan for A→B AND B→A (direct) and A→B→C→A (transitive)\n   361|4. Resolution: extract shared interface into ENABLER-NNN\n   362|   - Scope: contract/interface definition ONLY (no business logic)\n   363|   - Both dependents implement against the contract independently\n   364|   - Add ENABLER-NNN to epics section with type: enabler, complexity: S\n   365|   - Log in circular_resolutions\n   366|\n   367|### Topological Sequencing\n   368|1. Compute topological order from dependency graph (post circular resolution)\n   369|2. Map to phases using PRD mvp_phasing + dependency constraints\n   370|3. Validate BY SCAN, not by inspection: for EVERY epic_to_epic edge, assert\n   371|   `position(blocker) < position(blocked)` against the emitted `topological_order`,\n   372|   and write one `ordering_proof` row per edge. Report `edges_checked` alongside the\n   373|   violation count — a violation count with no denominator cannot be audited, and a\n   374|   check that never enumerates edges cannot fail.\n   375|4. If violation → auto-correct, re-run the scan, and log\n   376|5. If PRD execution plan conflicts with dependency-aware sequencing →\n   377|   dependency-aware takes precedence, note conflict for PRD update\n   378|\n   379|### Consolidation Pass (Before Writing)\n   380|After generating all sections:\n   381|1. Verify every PRD ID appears exactly once in `prd_id_ownership` with disposition\n   382|   `owned`, `cross_cutting`, or `deferred`.\n   383|2. Every epic with status: unaligned → alignment_gaps in open_questions\n   384|3. Every persona with 0 epics → alignment_gaps\n   385|4. Every goal with 0 epics → alignment_gaps\n   386|5. Every assumption → assumptions_to_validate\n   387|6. PRD open questions → never re-listed (cite their `OQ-` ids from the prompt blocks in the body)\n   388|7. Compute summary counts\n   389|8. Set top-level status: `complete` if zero pending_inputs AND zero alignment_gaps.\n   390|   Otherwise: `draft`.\n   391|\n   392|### Structured Contract Rules\n   393|- Native epics emitted by this skill declare `contract_format: structured`.\n   394|- `prd_source_hash` is sha256 from PRD `content_hash` when present; otherwise compute\n   395|  sha256 over the loaded PRD content for this run. Do not use mtime.\n   396|- `prd_id_ownership` covers every PRD ID from FR/NFR/JTBD/KPI/RSK/ASM/DEP/P/persona\n   397|  and PRD `literal_registry`.\n   398|- `open_questions` rows use `affected_ids`, `blocking`, and `fallback_behavior`.\n   399|- Source references use stable section/ID anchors, not line numbers.\n   400|\n   401|### REPAIR Mode\n   402|- Load existing spec file\n   403|- Apply REPAIR_DIRECTIVES to targeted sections/epic IDs\n   404|- Preserve existing EPIC IDs. New epics continue from max(existing) + 1.\n   405|- Retired IDs never reused.\n   406|- If upstream PRD changed (new/removed FRs): rebuild affected epics\n   407|- Rebuild dependencies from scratch if any epic added/removed\n   408|- Rebuild sequencing from updated dependency graph\n   409|- Rebuild open_questions from scratch (always reflects current state)\n   410|- Increment version, log changes\n   411|\n   412|### Won't Have / Deferred\n   413|PRD out_of_scope items and wont_have FRs MUST appear in sequencing.deferred.\n   414|This prevents scope creep by making exclusions explicit and traceable.\n   415|If PRD has no out-of-scope → note in open_questions.\n   416|\n</file>","isError":false,"durationMs":8}}
