[08:56:57] {"type":"thinking_delta","payload":{"delta":"Now the final section: open_questions. What did THIS run raise?\n\nPer the rules: PRD open questions (PI-01..PI-11) are inherited — never re-listed. Assumptions ASM-01..ASM-07 are inherited too (they're in the prompt's OPEN QUESTIONS block as OQ- ids). So what did THIS run genuinely raise?\n\nDecision test: does a downstream artifact get built differently depending on the answer, and inputs don't contain it?\n\nCandidates:\n1. EPIC-06 (history retrieval) has no committed endpoint contract — that's OQ-025246e3, inherited. Cited, not re-raised.\n2. EPIC-08 documentation enabler: no FR trace, KPI-backed — that's an alignment note, but it passes the enabler gate with KPI-04 trace, so not unaligned. No gap.\n3. Theme T-04 grouping inferred — assumption ASM-E01? The template shows assumptions_to_validate for theme grouping. T-04 groups an FR-traced epic and a KPI-traced enabler; grouping is inferred. This is a genuine assumption THIS run made. I could register ASM-E01: theme grouping inferred. That's a legitimate assumptions_to_validate row.\n4. Epic sizing: all epics ≤10 stories, no XL. Fine.\n5. Priority distribution: must_have (5), should_have (1), could_have (2) — distributed. Fine.\n6. FR coverage: 10 of 10 mapped. 100%.\n7. NFR embedding: all 7 NFRs appear as DoD constraints. Verified via ownership table.\n8. Personas: all covered. Goals: all covered.\n9. Unaligned epics: none (EPIC-08 traces to KPI-04; EPIC-07 traces to FR-10 + KPI-01).\n\nSo open_questions: pending_inputs — none raised by this run (all PI-01..PI-11 are inherited). alignment_gaps — none. assumptions_to_validate — ASM-E01 (theme grouping inferred). \n\nShould I raise anything else? The MVP scope filter (Step 5): every epic must trace to a project-brief MVP bullet. Let me check: \n- EPIC-01 standard ops → brief §2 Standard Operations ✓\n- EPIC-02 calculate API → brief §4 ✓\n- EPIC-03 extensibility → brief §1/§2? Extensibility is in discovery transcript; brief mentions \"controlled evolution of numerical behavior\" §Overview/§1. Semantic overlap with brief §1 \"controlled evolution of numerical behavior\" ✓\n- EPIC-04 advanced ops → brief §2 Advanced Operations ✓\n- EPIC-05 history → brief §2 History Tracking ✓\n- EPIC-06 history retrieval → brief §4 History Retrieval ✓\n- EPIC-07 stateless service → brief §3 ✓\n- EPIC-08 documentation → brief §7 \"API contract documented for internal reuse\" ✓\n\nAll pass. No deferred_candidates.\n\nSo the open_questions section: pending_inputs empty (or note), alignment_gaps empty, assumptions_to_validate with ASM-E01. Summary counts. Status: complete? Rule: \"Set top-level status: complete if zero pending_inputs AND zero alignment_gaps. Otherwise: draft.\" With ASM-E01 in assumptions_to_validate — the rule says pending_inputs AND alignment_gaps only, so status: complete. Hmm, but assumptions exist. The rule as written: zero pending_inputs AND zero alignment_gaps → complete. I'll set status: complete.\n\nWait — but should ASM-E01 go into the sidecar _open_questions? Yes: every row of assumptions_to_validate is an assumption entry per §11.6.\n\nActually, is the theme grouping assumption worth raising? T-04 mixes FR-10 epic and KPI-04 enabler. It's a mild inferred grouping. The template's example shows ASM-E01 for inferred grouping. I'll include it — it's honest and one row.\n\nAlso should I flag anything about EPIC-06's pending endpoint? That's inherited (OQ-025246e3) — cited in the epic body already. Not re-raised.\n\nSidecar _open_questions: one entry (ASM-E01, kind: assumption).\n\nNow write open_questions section.","turnId":"c6bdf510-6efe-4431-9474-70d47e2e469b"}}
